    "alert_id": "ALERT_001",
    "title": "DTG-associated weight gain and pre-diabetes risk",
    "message": "Guidelines identify rapid weight gain as a risk factor for diabetes in PLHIV on ART. Patient gained 17kg (65→82kg) and BMI rose from 25.6 to 32.4 (obese class I) within 18 months of switching to DTG-based TLD. She now has pre-diabetic fasting glucose (118 mg/dL) and HbA1c (6.1%), plus acanthosis nigricans. DTG is strongly temporally linked: weight gain began after TLD initiation. Evidence against drug attribution: family history of Type 2 Diabetes is an independent contributor. Non-drug causes (dietary, behavioural) should also be considered. No clinician assessment or plan was documented today.",
    "issue_type": "toxicity",
    "severity": "high",
    "recommended_action": "Assess for DM using the guideline screening tool, counsel on lifestyle modification, and consider DTG-related metabolic effects. Document a formal management plan.",
