    "title": "Dyslipidemia and hypertension compounding metabolic risk",
    "message": "Guidelines note dyslipidemia as a risk factor for diabetes in PLHIV. Patient has an adverse lipid profile: total cholesterol 228 mg/dL, LDL 148 mg/dL, HDL 38 mg/dL, triglycerides 212 mg/dL. BP increased from 118/74 to 138/88 mmHg since TLD initiation, approaching hypertensive range. Obesity (BMI 32.4), pre-diabetes, dyslipidemia, and elevated BP together substantially increase cardiovascular risk. No clinician plan addresses these metabolic abnormalities.",
